in @prism
in @io/git
in @mirror/store
in @mirror/pack

# @peer — the substrate's peer carrier at glass altitude.
#
# Family-root for the parametric/open peer type that `~peer'<path>'`
# references resolve to. Resolves the two-peer-types collision Taut
# flagged in the 2026-06-24 substrate-pull scout (runner-up #3.1).
#
# === The two-peer altitudes ===
#
# @pack.peer (shards/pack.mirror:188) is the CLOSED variant:
#   `type peer = | mara | seam | glint | reed | taut`
#
# Transitional per Alex 2026-06-24: "the named peers in the pack
# (reed, mara etc) those won't live in the compiler itself. That's
# our structure and not the default shape." Substrate-vs-USE applied.
#
# @peer.peer (this shard) is the PARAMETRIC carrier:
#   the substrate-decl shape that EVERY pack's members must inhabit
#
# When @pack.peer goes parametric, it lifts to be typed against
# @peer.peer. The 5-name closed variant becomes one specific
# realization at the USE altitude; @peer is the SHAPE that ships.
#
# === G1 resolution (Alex 2026-06-25): ~peer composes ~git ===
#
# Alex confirmed today: "yes" — `~peer'<path>'` silently composes
# `~git'<path>'` for url/ssh forms. Two-cache risk dissolves; @peer
# is a typed LENS over @git, not a parallel resolver. Resolution
# flow:
#
#   ~peer'<dir>'
#     → @io/git resolves <dir> as a git ref (existing a1b507a shape)
#     → @peer.load(<dir>) reads <dir>/mirror.spec
#     → extracts the spec's pack{}.lead per peer-ACL §6.2 self-naming
#     → returns typed peer
#
# Single-hop resolution per peer-ACL §6.2 + O7 dissolution (the lead
# IS the peer's self-declaration; no transitive chase).
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - #84 (@pack multi-repo agent runtime; promoted): the @pack.peer
#   variant is the consumer-altitude instance; @peer (this shard) is
#   the substrate-altitude shape
# - #99 (mirror.spec IS λ₀; Alex-named, Mara canonical d0b6519):
#   the @peer carrier IS what mirror.spec's pack{}.lead field refers
#   TO at λ₀. Without @peer at substrate altitude, the lead-of-λ₀
#   reference has no type. This shard makes the reference well-typed.
# - peer-ACL spec §2.2 (`@peer` glass at peer-glass.md per Mara's 7
#   discovery hits): the existing peer-glass.md doc gave the load(dir)
#   signature; this shard makes it substrate-decl typecheck.
# - #58 (Fate IS optical inference): the @peer carrier composes with
#   @fate at runtime via the lead's spawn-and-probe relation; no
#   external LLM adapter needed.
#
# === Composition with @mirror/pack ===
#
# `shards/mirror/pack.mirror` (13328a3) declares `type mirror_pack_block
# = { lead: peer, bindings: ref, members: ref }`. The `lead: peer`
# field references @pack.peer (closed variant) currently; when @pack
# migrates to parametric, the lead field's type lifts to @peer.peer
# (this shard). The @mirror/pack substrate-decl admits both readings
# without surface change because `peer` is name-resolved at compose
# time against the in-scope @pack OR @peer family.

prism @peer {
  focus peer
  project peer
  split peer
  shift peer
  settle peer
}

# === The kind carrier ===
#
# Closed variant distinguishing peer altitudes. Per recognition #84
# pack-as-orchestra + the substrate-altitude composition rules:
#
#   human      — a Pack peer with a human body (Alex; future humans
#                joining a pack at peer altitude)
#   agent      — a Pack peer running on @fate inference (Reed, Mara,
#                Seam, Taut, Glint as our current realizations; ANY
#                substrate-aware agent more broadly)
#   substrate  — a non-Pack-peer substrate entity that consumes ~peer'…'
#                references at @mirror/pack altitude (e.g., a CI runner
#                consuming the spec's pack block; not itself a peer)
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the variant tag.
type kind = | human | agent | substrate

# === The peer carrier ===
#
# Three-field record at glass altitude. The fields:
#
#   home     — the peer's home repo path (the canonical-path-rule
#              anchor: ~peer'<home>' resolves through here per
#              CLAUDE.md home-symlink convention). Composes with @io/
#              git's `git_repository` carrier (shards/io/git.mirror).
#
#   lead_of  — list of mirror.spec paths where THIS peer is named
#              `lead` in the spec's pack{} block. The reverse-
#              relation of mirror_pack_block.lead. Used by audit (“who
#              answers the lambda shell for spec S” → search lead_of).
#              Substrate-typed as `ref` until tuple-list carrier
#              surfaces at @epistemologic.
#
#   kind     — the closed variant above. Required iff peer is
#              referenced as a pack member (mirror_pack_block.members
#              entries are all human|agent kind; substrate-kind peers
#              are NOT members).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the (home, lead_of, kind)
# triple. Two peer values with the same home but different kind are
# distinct (kind admission gates pack membership; the same home repo
# can host either a human or an agent presence over time, but at any
# given peer-value, the kind is fixed).
type peer = {
  home:     ref,
  lead_of:  ref,
  kind:     kind,
}

# === load — the peer resolver ===
#
# Lifts `~peer'<dir>'` references into typed peer values. The G1-
# composition with @io/git is encapsulated here: `load(dir, p)`
# internally invokes @io/git's `resolve_ref` against <dir> + reads
# <dir>/mirror.spec to extract pack{}.lead per peer-ACL §6.2.
#
# Returns imperfect(peer, ref, ref) per @glass discipline: success-
# variant carries the typed peer; failure variants carry the missing
# git-ref / missing-spec / malformed-pack-block / not-a-lead reasons
# (refined at species per @glass/imperfect conventions).
load(dir: ref, p: perturbation) -> imperfect(peer, ref, ref) { \ }

# === Forward-promised — NOT landed this tick ===
#
# - lead_of_well_formed(p: peer, perturbation) -> verdict
#     bilateral predicate; checks that p.lead_of entries actually
#     name p in their pack{}.lead. Closes the reverse-relation
#     invariant.
#
# - peer_coherent(p: peer, perturbation) -> verdict
#     composed bilateral per recognition #53 family (14th altitude
#     lift when it lands).

out @peer
out kind
out peer
out load
